# WORKFLOWS — start background jobs and check on them.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Pick the REST Client environment (bottom-right of VS Code). Check it before
#      sending anything that starts a job: it may be production.
#   2. Set @recipeId below when using section B.
#   3. Send a "START" request. Then send the "check" request directly below it.
#      It reads the instance ID from the START response, so you don't copy anything.
#   4. When a task fails, copy its taskId into @taskId and use section A.
# Labels (READ ONLY, START, AI…) are explained in README.md.
#
# NOT IN THIS FILE
#   Reimport a recipe from its URL or photos  → 11-recipe-reimport.rest
#   Backup, seed, disaster recovery           → 04-management.rest
#   Demo-mode capture and restore             → 08-demo-mode.rest
#
# Every workflow is defined in api/src/RecipeApi/Workflows/<workflow-id>.yaml.
# The trigger checks that required parameters are present and ignores extra ones.

@recipeId = 5a7f6de2-3473-4229-9575-6948f01c3126
@instanceId = 52ad4126-d444-4851-a51c-5791c11d055e
@taskId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# A. CHECK ON JOBS
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### A1. READ ONLY — Running and paused jobs
# Lists instances that are Processing or Paused. Pending jobs that have not
# started yet do not appear here.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/active
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### A2. READ ONLY — One job by instance ID (paste it into @instanceId)
# Shows the status of each task. Use the "check" requests in B and C for jobs
# started from this file.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### A3. READ ONLY — Why a task failed (paste it into @taskId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/tasks/{{taskId}}/diagnostics
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### A4. START — Retry a failed task (paste it into @taskId)
# Sets the task back to Pending and resumes its workflow from that task.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/tasks/{{taskId}}/reset
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# B. ONE RECIPE (uses @recipeId)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### B1. START + AI — Reindex search for one recipe (search text + embedding)
# The empty fingerprint forces the job to run even if the content has not changed.
# Completes without doing anything if the recipe is deleted, has no extracted
# text, or has no search record yet. If it has no search record, run C1 instead.
# In demo mode it rebuilds the search text but does not create an embedding.
# @name reindexRecipe
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/index-recipe-search/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {
    "recipeId": "{{recipeId}}",
    "fingerprint": ""
  }
}

### B1 check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{reindexRecipe.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### B2. START + AI — Regenerate the description
# Steps: generate description → sync recipe → categorize recipe.
# @name regenerateDescription
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/recipe-description-regeneration/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {
    "recipeId": "{{recipeId}}"
  }
}

### B2 check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{regenerateDescription.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### B3. START + AI — Regenerate the hero image
# Uses the recipe endpoint, which applies the demo-mode AI guard.
# It does not return an instance ID. Use A1 to watch the job.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/recipes/{{recipeId}}/hero/regenerate
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### B4. START + AI — Recategorize ingredients
# Steps: categorize ingredients → mark recipe ready.
# @name recategorizeIngredients
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/recategorize-ingredients/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {
    "recipeId": "{{recipeId}}"
  }
}

### B4 check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{recategorizeIngredients.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### B5. START + AI — Classify vegetarian / non-vegetarian
# @name classifyVegetarian
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/classify-recipe-vegetarian/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {
    "recipeId": "{{recipeId}}"
  }
}

### B5 check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{classifyVegetarian.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}


# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# C. ALL RECIPES (backfills — each batch queues the next batch)
# A batch's check only shows that batch. Keep checking A1 until no instance of
# the workflow remains.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### C1. START — Search reconciliation (find recipes whose search is missing or stale)
# Scans ready recipes in batches. Queues B1-style reindex jobs only for recipes
# whose search is missing, stale, or failed. Those reindex jobs call AI.
# There is no per-recipe option; use B1 for one recipe.
# @name searchReconciliation
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/search-reconciliation/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {}
}

### C1 check — result: scanned, queued, cursor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{searchReconciliation.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### C2. START + AI — Vegetarian classification backfill
# Classifies recipes that are not classified yet and skips the others.
# Queues one B5 job per recipe, 25 recipes per batch.
# After A1 shows no backfill left, run C3 and then C1.
# @name vegetarianBackfill
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/vegetarian-classification-backfill/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {}
}

### C2 check — result: total, classified, unknown, vegetarian, nonVegetarian, queued
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{vegetarianBackfill.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### C3. START — Vegetarian classification counts (no AI, changes nothing)
# @name vegetarianStatus
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/vegetarian-classification-status/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {}
}

### C3 check — result: total, classified, unknown, vegetarian, nonVegetarian
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{vegetarianStatus.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

### C4. START — Servings backfill (no AI)
# Fills only missing servings counts from stored yield data and keeps existing
# counts. Requires the servings schema migration to be applied first.
# @name servingsBackfill
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/recipe-servings-backfill/trigger
Content-Type: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}

{
  "parameters": {}
}

### C4 check — result: examined, updated, unresolved, changed, nextCursor
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/workflows/instances/{{servingsBackfill.response.body.$.data.instanceId}}
Accept: application/json
X-Hearth-Secret: {{hearthSecret}}
